sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-08> delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/cell-geometry-thompson1917-ch07-08> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/cell-geometry-thompson1917-ch07-08> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Exploratory cell-geometry test of thompson1917-ch07-08 on 5 images: supports" ;
    dct:description "Exploratory test of thompson1917-ch07-08: If hexagons are regular only where cells are equal in size, tissues with more uniform cell areas have a larger fraction of six-sided cells, and within a tissue cells in more size-heterogeneous neighbourhoods depart more from six sides.\n\nResult: -0.9 (Spearman rho, tissue area CV vs fraction of six-sided interior cells; n = 5; p = 0.0374).\n\nCriterion: Exploratory, not pre-registered: the images were segmented and inspected before the pass criterion was written. Treat the verdict as hypothesis-generating; a pre-registered replication on new images is needed before it counts as a test. Supports if Spearman rho between tissue area CV and fraction of six-sided interior cells is <= -0.7 across usable tissues; mixed if between -0.7 and 0; refutes if >= 0.\n\nInterpretation: Tests the size-uniformity part only; 'forces uniform' is not measured. This is a second, multi-tissue attempt; the pre-registered within-RPE test of the same claim is test-data/claim-tests/thompson-growth-form/thompson1917-ch07-08/result.json." ;
    schema:value "-0.9"^^xsd:double ;
    schema:unitText "Spearman rho, tissue area CV vs fraction of six-sided interior cells" ;
    delphi:pValue "0.0374"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:statisticalTest "Spearman rank correlation across 5 tissues, two-sided" ;
    rdfs:comment "Exploratory, not pre-registered: the images were segmented and inspected before the pass criterion was written. Treat the verdict as hypothesis-generating; a pre-registered replication on new images is needed before it counts as a test.\nOnly 5 tissues; the across-tissue correlation rests on five points.\nThe random-Voronoi control shows the same within-image relation, so the result is a property of space-filling partitions in general and says nothing about forces." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/0d6f11c2931e2a6e86516c68a8e05ad599c76355/test-data/claim-tests/thompson-growth-form/thompson1917-ch07-08/cellpose-multi-tissue/result.json> ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-human-corneal-endothelium> ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-drosophila-compound-eye> ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-physcomitrella-leaf> ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-festuca-leaf-epidermis> ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-aloe-leaf-epidermis> ;
    schema:additionalProperty sub:value0 ;
    schema:additionalProperty sub:value1 ;
    schema:additionalProperty sub:value2 ;
